<title>SINGAPORE: Singapore April industrial output rises 1.1 pct.</title>
<headline>Singapore April industrial output rises 1.1 pct.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-06-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Singapore's total manufacturing output rose by 1.1 percent in April compared to the same month the year before, after falling a revised 6.9 per cent in March, the Economic Development Board (EDB) said on Monday.</p>
<p>Table of selected Singapore industries:</p>
<p>				    (pct change over previous year)</p>
<p>				    Apr 97	 Mar 97	  Feb 96</p>
<p>   *Total manufacturing	 1.1	   -6.9	   -3.5</p>
<p>    Electronics		   3.1	  -12.0	   -6.2</p>
<p>    Petroleum products	-13.6	  -14.3	   -8.9</p>
<p>    Pharmaceuticals	    15.2	   -0.9	   29.4</p>
<p>    Industrial chemicals     13.8	   13.5	   11.3</p>
<p>    Petrochemicals	     11.1	   29.2	   48.6</p>
<p>    Machinery x-electronics  -3.3	    3.6	   -9.1</p>
<p>    Transport equipment	 6.3	    1.5	   -9.2</p>
<p>    Fabricated metals	 -10.6	   -9.7	   -6.0</p>
<p>    Printing/publishing	 6.3	    1.5	   -3.4</p>
<p>    Food &amp; Beverages	   -1.8	  -11.9	  -15.3</p>
<p>    Electrical machines	-1.7	   -0.7	  -10.7</p>
<p>    Plastic products	  -10.3	  -19.4	  -21.7</p>
<p>* Total manufacturing output excludes rubber processing.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703199)</p>
